+# ::a1 The office coffee machine should go
+
+::a2 This is a constructed debate, made to demonstrate and test the platform for answers that do not point at a single sentence, but at a range of sentences or at a few words inside one. ::a3 Its topic is deliberately trivial, so that nothing distracts from where the answers point.
+
+::a4 I would like to propose that we get rid of the capsule machine in the kitchen and switch to a kettle and a French press. ::a5 The machine costs us around forty euros a month in capsules alone. ::a6 It breaks roughly twice a year, and every repair leaves us without coffee for a week. ::a7 The capsules are not recyclable in any practical sense, whatever the packaging says. ::a8 And the coffee it produces is, to be blunt, not very good.
+
+::a9 A kettle and a press would cost us maybe sixty euros once, take up less space, and be impossible to break in any interesting way. ::a10 The obvious objection is that it takes three minutes longer in the morning. ::a11 I think that is a price worth paying. ::a12 If anyone disagrees, now would be the time to say so.
